# The step of bv_make_1, the constructor of a BallVector with one-limb centers (milestone2.md,
# "BallVector", "Values"): a center that the program gives, guarded (rule R3) as the constructors of a
# Ball are. Its value is the center itself: guard(c) is RN(c + 0), which is c (a zero made +0), and an
# infinity or a NaN stays what it is, which the finish of the constructor tests.
kernel:        bv_center_entry_1
input:         c
output:        z
value:         c
ensures:       rounded z nearest
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/BvNegMake.v bv_center_entry_1_correct
ieee_bridge_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeBvNegMake.v bv_center_entry_1_ieee_bridge
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeBvNegMake.v bv_center_entry_1_ieee_lead
source:        the guard of a constructor (milestone2.md, BallVector, Values)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge

z = guard(c)
